{"availability":"available","full":"QuangCler/ghostconvmae-face-demo","name":"ghostconvmae-face-demo","description":"ConvMAE-Base vs Ghost+ConvMAE side by side on CelebA, CASIA, SCface, LFW and an ImageNet-1K linear probe - PyTorch or TensorRT, with per-model latency and VRAM.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-25T12:44:01Z","updated":"2026-08-27T17:52:27Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://quangcler.github.io/ghostconvmae-face-demo/","topics":["computer-vision","face-recognition","gradio","model-deployment","onnx","pytorch","tensorrt","vision-transformer"],"demo":"https://quangcler.github.io/ghostconvmae-face-demo/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:59.036Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:59.036Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:59.036Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:34:59.036Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Interactive demo comparing the two deployed backbones — ConvMAE-Base vs Ghost+ConvMAE — side by side on four face tasks plus an ImageNet-1K linear-probe tab. Each tab has a short description of what the models do, an in-UI image picker (choose a sample straight from that task's dataset, or drop your own — the chosen filename is shown), and the two models' predictions next to each other. You can switch the inference backend between native PyTorch and a TensorRT engine in the UI. Runs on a laptop: a small CUDA GPU (e.g. GTX 1650, 4 GB) or plain CPU (auto-detected). Switching tabs clears the…","Only the two convolution/Transformer arms (ConvMAE-Base, Ghost+ConvMAE) are shown — in every tab, including the linear-probe one. The Ghost+ForwardMamba and Ghost+BiMamba arms are deliberately excluded from this laptop demo: their Stage-3 Mamba blocks need the CUDA-only mambassm selective-scan kernels, which do not install on the target GTX 1650, and the selective-scan op has no ONNX/TensorRT path — so those arms can neither run in PyTorch here nor be exported to an engine.","The full four-arm linear-probe deployment runs on a CUDA server, not here: baseline/ghost through PyTorch + TensorRT and the two Mamba arms through PyTorch only. Its tool (scripts/demodeployinfer.py) and the Mamba classifier factories live in the research repo, inference-efficient-convmae."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuangCler/ghostconvmae-face-demo/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e6997bba58b55d3ddd27c281da96289cb5ccd7fea2cad79c60179975655edebb","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:59.159Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:59.159Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Interactive demo comparing the two deployed backbones — ConvMAE-Base vs Ghost+ConvMAE — side by side on four face tasks plus an ImageNet-1K linear-probe tab. Each tab has a short description of what the models do, an in-UI image picker (choose a sample straight from that task's dataset, or drop your own — the chosen filename is shown), and the two models' predictions next to each other. You can switch the inference backend between native PyTorch and a TensorRT engine in the UI. Runs on a laptop: a small CUDA GPU (e.g. GTX 1650, 4 GB) or plain CPU (auto-detected). Switching tabs clears the…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuangCler/ghostconvmae-face-demo/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"e6997bba58b55d3ddd27c281da96289cb5ccd7fea2cad79c60179975655edebb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuangCler/ghostconvmae-face-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:59.159Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-27T17:52:27Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/QuangCler/ghostconvmae-face-demo/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:59.160Z","hash":"e6997bba58b55d3ddd27c281da96289cb5ccd7fea2cad79c60179975655edebb","originalBytes":23086,"storedBytes":23086,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["tensorrt","python","pytorch","